# Salt-e PA - optional Jira module scheduled jobs (templates)
#
# Both jobs are safe to register at any time: each one no-ops and exits 0
# unless the module is opted in (PA_JIRA_ENABLED truthy, or jira.enabled: true
# in memory/workstream_config.yml). Nothing runs on a fresh clone.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Replace <REPO_ROOT> with your clone's absolute path, for example
#      /home/you/salt-e-pa (Linux/macOS) or C:/Users/you/salt-e-pa (Windows).
#   2. Export the module env vars so the scheduled run resolves credentials the
#      same way your interactive shell does. Credentials are environment-only:
#        PA_JIRA_ENABLED=1
#        PA_JIRA_BASE_URL=<JIRA_BASE_URL>
#        PA_JIRA_EMAIL=<JIRA_ACCOUNT_EMAIL>
#        PA_JIRA_API_TOKEN=<JIRA_API_TOKEN>
#        PA_JIRA_PROJECT_KEYS=<KEY_A>,<KEY_B>
#      Put them in the crontab header (KEY=value lines above the jobs) or source
#      them inline. Never commit the token to this file or any other.
#   3. See modules/jira/README.md for the full variable reference.

# Daily Jira sync at 07:50 local
50 7 * * * cd <REPO_ROOT> && python modules/jira/jira_sync.py

# Monthly Jira health audit at 08:20 local on the 1st of the month
20 8 1 * * cd <REPO_ROOT> && python modules/jira/jira_health_audit.py

# Named-scheduler task-ID prefix convention (if you use one instead of bare
# crontab lines): give every task ID a short workspace-unique prefix so IDs
# never collide with other projects on the same machine, for example:
#   mypa-jira-sync
#   mypa-jira-health-audit
